1
00:06:27,692 --> 00:06:33,692
Groucho & Cavett is a documentary film directed by Robert S. Bader.

2
00:12:55,384 --> 00:13:01,384
Discover the enduring friendship between television personality Dick
Cavett and his mentor iconic comedian Groucho Marx.

3
00:19:23,076 --> 00:19:29,076
Their relationship is chronicled through interviews with Cavett,
archival footage and interviews with George Burns and others.

4
00:25:50,769 --> 00:25:56,769
Self, played by Dick Cavett.

5
00:32:18,461 --> 00:32:24,461
Self (archive footage), played by Groucho Marx.

6
00:38:46,153 --> 00:38:52,153
Self (archive footage), played by Jack Paar.

7
00:45:13,846 --> 00:45:19,846
Self (archive footage), played by E.Y. Harburg.

8
00:51:41,538 --> 00:51:47,538
Self (archive footage), played by Woody Allen.

9
00:58:09,230 --> 00:58:15,230
Self (archive footage), played by Shelley Winters.

10
01:04:36,923 --> 01:04:42,923
Richard Alva Cavett ( KAV-it; born November 19, 1936) is an American
television personality, comedian and former talk show host.

11
01:11:04,615 --> 01:11:10,615
He appeared regularly on nationally broadcast television in the
United States from the 1960s through the 2000s.

12
01:17:32,307 --> 01:17:38,307
In later years, Cavett has written an online column for The New York Times, promoted DVDs of his former shows as well as a book of his Times columns, and hosted replays of his TV interviews with Bette Davis, Lucille Ball, Salvador Dalí, Lee Marvin, Groucho Marx, Katharine Hepburn, Judy
Garland, Marlon Brando, Orson Welles, Woody Allen, Ingmar Bergman, Jean-Luc Godard, Robert Mitchum, John Lennon, George Harrison, Jimi Hendrix, Richard Burton, Sophia Loren, Marcello Mastroianni, Kirk Douglas, Mae West and Bobby Fischer, among others, on Turner Classic Movies.
